WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.017 --> 00:00:04.581
(bluesy rock music)

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:06.786
- You're doing it again.

00:00:06.786 --> 00:00:08.376
- Doing what again?

00:00:08.376 --> 00:00:09.665
- My therapist says.

00:00:09.665 --> 00:00:10.641
- Oh my God.

00:00:10.641 --> 00:00:12.775
- [Voiceover] You haven't
moved in like three days.

00:00:12.775 --> 00:00:15.631
You kinda just walk around moaning.

00:00:15.631 --> 00:00:17.223
- Ugggghhh.

00:00:17.913 --> 00:00:19.534
Uuuuugh!

00:00:20.204 --> 00:00:21.465
- What?

00:00:21.465 --> 00:00:23.775
- Nothing. Just, everything.

00:00:23.775 --> 00:00:25.680
Yeah, it's that time of year.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.227
- The most wonderful time of the year?

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:31.923
(bouncy, electronic
version of "Jingle Bells")

00:00:31.923 --> 00:00:33.594
- Oh, December gloom.

00:00:33.594 --> 00:00:35.848
When you feel sad and anxious,

00:00:35.848 --> 00:00:40.455
and empty, hopeless, helpless, worthless.

00:00:40.455 --> 00:00:42.133
Guilty, irritable.

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:43.966
- Yeah, you're S-A-D.

00:00:43.966 --> 00:00:45.326
- Yeah, sad, right.

00:00:45.326 --> 00:00:47.381
- No. Seasonal Affective Disorder.

00:00:47.381 --> 00:00:48.587
- Oh my God.

00:00:48.587 --> 00:00:50.617
Stop it with your therapy terms.

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:51.755
- OK, my therapist says.

00:00:51.755 --> 00:00:52.556
- My therapist says.

00:00:52.556 --> 00:00:54.634
My therapist says. My therapist says.

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:55.876
- I don't sound like that.

00:00:55.876 --> 00:00:56.979
- My therapist says.

00:00:56.979 --> 00:01:01.336
- OK, my good friend who has
a PhD says it's perfectly

00:01:01.336 --> 00:01:03.373
normal to feel this way
during the holidays.

00:01:03.373 --> 00:01:04.738
I go through it every year.

00:01:04.738 --> 00:01:06.465
Don't want to get out of bed.

00:01:06.465 --> 00:01:09.692
Seeing everyone super
happy with their families.

00:01:09.692 --> 00:01:11.550
Mournfully opening the present

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.379
you got for your ex last year.

00:01:14.164 --> 00:01:16.774
- Yeah, it's called December gloom.

00:01:16.774 --> 00:01:20.172
- But, going to therapy
helped me see that there were

00:01:20.172 --> 00:01:22.072
larger issues there.

00:01:22.072 --> 00:01:25.031
- Anxiety, co-dependency,
emotional hoarding.

00:01:25.031 --> 00:01:27.359
- But they just, you know, get intensified

00:01:27.359 --> 00:01:29.101
during the holidays 'cause
there's such a focus

00:01:29.101 --> 00:01:30.608
on happiness.

00:01:30.608 --> 00:01:33.072
- I just don't wanna
become one of those people.

00:01:33.072 --> 00:01:33.885
You know?

00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:35.871
- An emotionally responsible person?

00:01:35.871 --> 00:01:36.771
Yeah, they suck.

00:01:36.771 --> 00:01:39.277
- One of those people
who write off their flaws

00:01:39.277 --> 00:01:41.460
by labeling it something clinical.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.422
You know, like, oh Jimmy,

00:01:43.422 --> 00:01:46.136
Jimmy, he's workin' on
it, but he has assholes.

00:01:46.136 --> 00:01:48.284
- Oh yeah he started a fight
with all the other dads

00:01:48.284 --> 00:01:49.620
at his son's soccer game.

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:50.328
- What are you gonna do?

00:01:50.328 --> 00:01:51.386
He has assholes.

00:01:51.386 --> 00:01:52.766
- Assholes runs in his family.

00:01:52.766 --> 00:01:54.058
- He's doin' his best.

00:01:54.058 --> 00:01:56.194
- You know he cheats on
his wife and he beats her,

00:01:56.194 --> 00:01:57.204
but what are you gonna do?

00:01:57.204 --> 00:01:59.085
He has assholes, he's workin' on it.

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:00.989
- Oh or like when people will just like

00:02:00.989 --> 00:02:04.017
misdiagnose themselves for
something more serious,

00:02:04.017 --> 00:02:04.516
you know?

00:02:04.516 --> 00:02:05.076
- Yeah.

00:02:05.076 --> 00:02:05.542
- Like.

00:02:05.542 --> 00:02:07.340
- Until the new season
of New Girl comes out,

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:08.869
I'm like depressed.

00:02:08.869 --> 00:02:10.308
- Yeah no you're not.

00:02:10.308 --> 00:02:11.416
- No you're not, bitch.

00:02:11.416 --> 00:02:13.021
- No, you love adorkable television.

00:02:13.021 --> 00:02:15.762
You don't have a
crippling mental disorder.

00:02:15.762 --> 00:02:19.303
- But, you know there are people who do,

00:02:19.303 --> 00:02:21.521
who once they go to therapy,

00:02:21.521 --> 00:02:23.445
it starts to get better.

00:02:23.445 --> 00:02:24.725
- It helps you?

00:02:24.725 --> 00:02:25.979
- Hell yeah.

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:28.533
Especially when I want
the perfect text response.

00:02:28.533 --> 00:02:30.169
OK, so that's what she said to me,

00:02:30.169 --> 00:02:31.565
but what should I say back?

00:02:31.565 --> 00:02:35.015
- Mmm. Maybe something like, "I hear you."

00:02:36.385 --> 00:02:38.606
- Mm-K. All right.

00:02:38.606 --> 00:02:39.974
I'll do it.

00:02:39.974 --> 00:02:41.197
- Good.

00:02:43.325 --> 00:02:44.764
Will you also clean this shit up,

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:45.764
'cause I live here too,

00:02:45.764 --> 00:02:48.898
and you're kinda being an asshole.

00:02:48.898 --> 00:02:49.724
- Oh, well I.

00:02:49.724 --> 00:02:50.342
- [Voiceover] Thanks.

00:02:50.342 --> 00:02:52.043
- I have assholes though.

00:02:52.043 --> 00:02:52.703
- [Voiceover] Shut up.

00:02:52.703 --> 00:02:54.108
- You'll see, I'll got to your therapist.

00:02:54.108 --> 00:02:57.010
Let you know I have messies.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.332
I have messy disease.

00:02:58.332 --> 00:02:59.952
I'm just messy.

00:02:59.952 --> 00:03:00.665
Sorry.

